§§ `A7 — one occurrence (src:542-544, 685-687, 812-814)`

GIVEN label IS A STRING, exposure IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A `A claim against an insured`
`a harm of occurrence` label `with exposure` exposure MEANS
    `A claim against an insured` WITH
        `the person claimed against`                                      IS `the named insured`
        `the harm`                                                        IS `bodily injury, sickness or disease sustained by a person`
        `the date the injury occurs`                                      IS YMD 2026 6 1
        `the date of the occurrence`                                      IS YMD 2026 6 1
        `the occurrence`                                                  IS label
        `the general conditions of exposure`                              IS exposure
        `the date the claim was first made in writing against an insured` IS NOTHING
        `the date an insured first became aware of circumstances which may give rise to the claim` IS NOTHING
        `the date written notice of those circumstances was given to the Company` IS NOTHING
        `the claim series`                                                IS NOTHING
        `the findings`                                                    IS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the harms of` (`a harm of occurrence` "leak in March" `with exposure` (JUST "fumes from the plant")) `and of` (`a harm of occurrence` "leak in May" `with exposure` (JUST "fumes from the plant")) `count as one occurrence for the limits`
#ASSERT NOT `the harms of` (`a harm of occurrence` "leak in March" `with exposure` (JUST "fumes from the plant")) `and of` (`a harm of occurrence` "leak in May" `with exposure` (JUST "noise from the plant")) `count as one occurrence for the limits`
#ASSERT NOT `the harms of` (`a harm of occurrence` "leak in March" `with exposure` NOTHING) `and of` (`a harm of occurrence` "leak in May" `with exposure` NOTHING) `count as one occurrence for the limits`
#ASSERT `the harms of` (`a harm of occurrence` "the collapse" `with exposure` NOTHING) `and of` (`a harm of occurrence` "the collapse" `with exposure` NOTHING) `count as one occurrence for the limits`

